libwebrtc-rs-js: cherry-picked from upstream WebRTC main
96270440dc37560b2de2ee3dc82c13be610e6ace
(https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/96270440dc37560b2de2ee3dc82c13be610e6ace),
which isn't in M150 (branch-heads/7871). Without it, addTransceiver() after
close() builds its media channel from the Call that Close() already
destroyed: a use-after-free, which crashed test/native/fake-native-drift.test.ts
(SIGSEGV in WebRtcVoiceSendChannel's constructor). The upstream commit's unit
test is left out; we don't build tests.

commit 96270440dc37560b2de2ee3dc82c13be610e6ace
Author: Tommi <tommi@webrtc.org>
Date:   Wed Oct 21 12:12:37 2026 +0200

    Fail AddTransceiver with INVALID_STATE when closed
    
    AddTransceiver() had no closed-state check, so after Close() the new
    transceiver created its media channels with the already destroyed Call.
    Return INVALID_STATE instead, as AddTrack() does and the spec requires.
    
    Fixed: webrtc:576148431
